================================================================================
                              DATA DISCLAIMER
================================================================================

This project uses Formula 1 timing data obtained through the FastF1 library
(https://github.com/theOehrly/Fast-F1), which is released under MIT License.

FastF1 accesses publicly available timing data broadcast during live F1 
sessions. This data is not obtained through official F1 APIs or paid services.


USAGE CONDITIONS
----------------

1. This project is for ACADEMIC and EDUCATIONAL purposes only
2. No commercial use is intended or permitted
3. No raw F1 data is redistributed - only aggregated analysis results
4. The trained models are derivative works based on statistical patterns


INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY NOTICE
----------------------------

Formula 1, F1, FIA Formula One World Championship, Grand Prix, and related 
marks are trademarks of Formula One Licensing BV.

This project is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to:
- Formula One Management (FOM)
- Formula One Licensing BV
- Federation Internationale de l'Automobile (FIA)
- Any F1 team or driver

Per Formula 1 Guidelines (https://www.formula1.com/en/information/guidelines):
"Limited use of Other Intellectual Property Rights for educational purposes 
may be acceptable where the use is justified, limited, and non-commercial."

This project falls under educational/academic fair use as:
- It is a university thesis project
- No F1 logos, images, or branded content are used
- Only statistical/numerical timing data is processed
- Output consists solely of ML model predictions and analysis


FASTF1 LIBRARY
--------------

FastF1 is an open-source project (MIT License) maintained since 2020.
Repository: https://github.com/theOehrly/Fast-F1
Documentation: https://docs.fastf1.dev/

FastF1's own disclaimer states:
"FastF1 and this website are unofficial and are not associated in any way 
with the Formula 1 companies."

Hundreds of academic and open-source projects use FastF1 for F1 data analysis
without reported legal issues from Formula One Management.


